  "title": "Basics 1",
  "description": "Learn your very first Chinese words and sentences! Meet people, name foods, and start talking about what you eat and drink.",
  "guidebook": "Welcome to your first Chinese lesson! 🎉\n\n**Nouns have no articles** in Chinese. There is no \"a,\" \"an,\" or \"the\" — 男人 means both \"a man\" and \"the man.\"\n\n**Subject + 是 (shì) + Noun** is the basic \"to be\" sentence. 是 means \"am/is/are.\" Example: 我是女孩 (I am a girl).\n\n**Verbs don't conjugate.** 吃 (chī, to eat) and 喝 (hē, to drink) stay the same no matter who does the action. Just say: 我喝水 (I drink water).\n\n**Word order** is usually Subject + Verb + Object, just like English: 我吃面包 (I eat bread).\n\n**Tones matter!** Mandarin has 4 tones plus a neutral tone. The pinyin shows tones with marks (ā, á, ǎ, à). Practice them out loud — they change meanings!\n\nLet's go! 🚀",
